# Excludes from the Docker build context shipped to the daemon.
# Anything matched here is NOT visible inside the build, regardless of
# whether the Dockerfile would have COPY'd it. Trimming the context
# keeps the per-build upload small and stops a stray .env from
# accidentally landing in an image layer.

# Workspace install artifacts — rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache

# Rust build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image by the rust-builder stage.
worker/target

# Local environment files — secrets. Production env lives in Fly.io secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs.
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Test surfaces — never executed at runtime.
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/e2e
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Per-project docs — readable on GitHub, not needed in the runtime image.
docs/
**/README.md
CHANGELOG.md
PLAN.md
PROGRESS.md
DECISIONS.md
AGENT_NOTES.md
CRITIQUE-*.md

# The build / deploy descriptors themselves — they tell the build what
# to do; they do not belong inside the resulting image.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
fly.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Git metadata — not needed at runtime, and a stray fragment of the
# repo's history in a layer is a leak surface.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Misc per-project ignores.
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
**/.next/cache
